HP's Photos & Videos (com.palm.app.photos), as modernized by webOS Archive for webOS Community
Edition: version 3.2.0, from the webOS CE project's tree
(https://github.com/webOSArchive/webOS-Community-Edition/tree/main/apps/com.palm.app.photos,
commit d3ccfed), without HP's development leftovers (spec/, Gemfile*, Rakefile, Makefile*,
ci_build.sh, .rvmrc), which CE's packager drops too. Over Palm's 3.0.8001 it adds Synergy
Revival cloud sources, the exhibition slideshow's clock and remembered timing, the file name in
the single-photo toolbar, videos handed to the CE Videos app (or played in its own player when
that app isn't installed), and a rotate and crop editor whose Save goes through webOS CE's
org.webosarchive.photos.service (laid into the webOS root by AndroidLuna/fetch-assets.sh).

The original is copyright Palm, Inc. / Hewlett-Packard, never released under an open licence;
distributed by Lunacy as abandonware, like Mojo, the Prelude fonts and the TouchPad wallpapers:
no owner has asserted rights since webOS was discontinued. The 3.2.0 changes are webOS
Archive's.

The app's files are here exactly as the package carries them, and Lunacy does not change them
(rule 5 in CLAUDE.md). It lists what webOS's media index holds (MediaIndex.kt answers it from
the files under /media/internal, Android's Pictures, DCIM and Movies among them) and shows the
thumbnails Palm's photos service makes, which Lunacy also ships. A change Lunacy needs in the
app is made in the webOS CE project and comes here with its next release.
